{
  "title": "51: Adh-Dhariyat الذاريات",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالذّٰرِيٰتِ ذَرْوًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAZ ZAAREYAATE ZARWAA.\nBy the scattering [winds] that scatter [the clouds];\nفَالْحٰمِلٰتِ وِقْرًا ۙ‏(2)\nFALHAAMELAATE WIQRAA.\nby the [rain] bearing [clouds] laden [with water];\nفَالْجٰرِيٰتِ يُسْرًا ۙ‏(3)\nFALJAAREYAATE YUSRAA.\nby [the ships] which move gently [on the sea];\nفَالْمُقَسِّمٰتِ اَمْرًا ۙ‏(4)\nFALMOQASSEMAATE AMRAA.\nby [the angels] who dispense [livelihood] by [His] command:\nاِنَّمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَصَادِقٌ ۙ‏(5)\nINNAMAA TOO-A’DOONA LA-SAADEQ.\nindeed what you are promised is true,\nوَّاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ لوَاقِعٌ ؕ‏(6)\nWA INNAD DEENA LA-WAAQE’.\nand indeed the retribution will surely come to pass!\nوَالسَّمَآءِ ذَاتِ الْحُبُكِ ۙ‏(7)\nWAS SAMAAA-E ZAATIL HOBOK.\nBy the sky full of adornment [with stars],\nاِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ قَوْلٍ مُّخْتَلِفٍ ۙ‏(8)\nINNAKUM LAFEE QAWLIM MUKHTALEF.\nindeed you are of different opinions!\nيُّؤْفَكُ عَنْهُ مَنْ اُفِكَ ؕ‏(9)\nYOAFAKO A’NHO MAN OFEK.\nHe who has been turned away [from the truth] is turned away from it.\nقُتِلَ الْخَرّٰصُوْنَۙ‏(10)\nQOTELAL KHARRAASOON.\nPerish the liars,\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ سَاهُوْنَۙ‏(11)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE GHAMRATIN SAAHOON.\nwho are heedless in a stupor!\nيَسْئَلُوْنَ اَيَّانَ يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(12)\nYAS-ALOONA AYYAANA YAWMUD DEEN.\nThey ask, ‘When will be the Day of Retribution?’\nيَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(13)\nYAWMA HUM A’LAN NAARE YUFTANOON.\nIt is the day when they will be tormented in the Fire,\nذُوْقُوْا فِتْنَتَكُمْؕ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(14)\nZOOQOO FITNATAKUM, HAAZAL LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TASTA’JELOON.\n[and will be told]: ‘Taste your torment. This is what you used to hasten.’\nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(15)\nINNAL MUTTAQEENA FEE JANNAATINW WA O’YOON.\nIndeed the Godwary will be amid gardens and springs,\nاٰخِذِيْنَ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَبْلَ ذٰلِكَ مُحْسِنِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nAAKHEZEENA MAA AATAAHUM RABBOHUM, INNAHUM KAANOO QABLA ZAALEKA MOHSENEEN.\nreceiving what their Lord has given them, for they had been virtuous aforetime.\nكَانُوْا قَلِيْلًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مَا يَهْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nKAANOO QALEELAM MENAL LAYLE MAA YAHJA-O’ON.\nThey used to sleep a little during the night,\nوَبِالْاَسْحَارِ هُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوْنَ‏(18)\nWA BIL-ASHAARE HUM YASTAGHFEROON.\nand at dawns they would plead for forgiveness,\nوَفِىْۤ اَمْوَالِهِمْ حَقٌّ لِّلسَّآئِلِ وَالْمَحْرُوْمِ‏(19)\nWA FEE AMWAALEHIM HAQQUL LIS-SAAA-ELE WAL MAHROOM.\nand there was a share in their wealth for the beggar and the deprived.\nوَفِى الْاَرْضِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّلْمُوْقِنِيْنَۙ‏(20)\nWA FIL ARZE AAYAATUL LIL-MOOQENEEN.\nIn the earth are signs for those who have conviction,\nوَفِىْۤ اَنْفُسِكُمْ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA FEE ANFOSEKUM, AFALAA TUBSEROON.\nand in your souls [as well]. Will you not then perceive?\nوَفِى السَّمَآءِ رِزْقُكُمْ وَمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA FIS SAMAAA-E RIZQOKUM WA MAA TOO-A’DOON.\nAnd in the sky is your provision and what you are promised.\nفَوَرَبِّ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ مِّثْلَ مَاۤ اَنَّكُمْ تَنْطِقُوْنَ‏(23)\nFAWA RABBIS SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE INNAHU LA-HAQQUM MISLA MAA ANNAKUM TANTEQOON.\nBy the Lord of the sky and the earth, it is indeed the truth, just as [it is a fact that] you speak.\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ ضَيْفِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الْمُكْرَمِيْنَ‌ۘ‏(24)\nHAL ATAAKA HADEESO ZAYFE IBRAAHEEMAL MUKRAMEEN.\nDid you receive the story of Abraham’s honoured guests?\nاِذْ دَخَلُوْا عَلَيْهِ فَقَالُوْا سَلٰمًا‌ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ ۚ قَوْمٌ مُّنْكَرُوْنَ‌‏(25)\nIZ DAKHALOO A’LAYHE FA-QAALOO SALAAMAA, QAALA SALAAM, QAWMUM MUNKAROON.\nWhen they entered into his presence, they said, ‘Peace!’ ‘Peace!’ He answered, ‘[You are] an unfamiliar folk.’\nفَرَاغَ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهٖ فَجَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ سَمِيْنٍۙ‏(26)\nFA-RAAGHA ELAA AHLEHI FA-JAAA-A BE-I’JLIN SAMEEN.\nThen he retired to his family and brought a fat [roasted] calf,\nفَقَرَّبَهٗۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَالَ اَلَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(27)\nFA-QARRABAHU ELAYHIM QAALA ALAA TAAKOLOON.\nand put it near them. He said, ‘Will you not eat?’\nفَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً‌ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ‌ ؕ وَبَشَّرُوْهُ بِغُلٰمٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(28)\nFA-AWJASA MINHUM KHEEFAH, QAALOO LAA TAKHAF, WA BASH-SHAROOHO BE-GHOLAAMIN A’LEEM.\nThen he felt a fear of them. They said, ‘Do not be afraid!’ and they gave him the good news of a wise son.\nفَاَقْبَلَتِ امْرَاَتُهٗ فِىْ صَرَّةٍ فَصَكَّتْ وَجْهَهَا وَقَالَتْ عَجُوْزٌ عَقِيْمٌ‏(29)\nFA-AQBALATIM RA-ATOHU FEE SARRATIN FA-SAKKAT WAJHAHAA WA QAALAT A’JOOZUN A’QEEM.\nThen his wife came forward crying [with joy]. She beat her face, and said, ‘A barren old woman!’\nقَالُوْا كَذٰلِكِ ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(30)\nQAALOO KAZAALEKE, QAALA RABBOK, INNAHU HOWAL HAKEEMUL A’LEEM.\nThey said, ‘So has your Lord said. Indeed He is the All-wise, the All-knowing.’\nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكُمْ اَيُّهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(31)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBOKUM AYYOHAL MURSALOON.\nHe said, ‘O messengers, what is now your errand?’\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمٍ مُّجْرِمِيْنَۙ‏(32)\nQAALOO INNAA URSILNAA ELAA QAWMIM MUJREMEEN.\nThey said, ‘We have been sent toward a guilty people,\nلِنُرْسِلَ عَلَيْهِمْ حِجَارَةً مِّنْ طِيْنٍۙ‏(33)\nLE-NURSELA A’LAYHIM HEJAARATAM MIN TEEN.\nthat We may rain upon them stones of clay,\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(34)\nMOSAWWAMATAN I’NDA RABBEKA LIL-MUSREFEEN.\nsent for the transgressors from your Lord.\nفَاَخْرَجْنَا مَنْ كَانَ فِيْهَا مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(35)\nFA-AKHRAJNAA MAN KAANA FEEHAA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nSo We picked out those who were in it of the faithful,\nفَمَا وَجَدْنَا فِيْهَا غَيْرَ بَيْتٍ مِّنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(36)\nFAMAA WAJADNAA FEEHAA GHAYRA BAYTIM MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nbut We did not find there other than one house of Muslims,\nوَتَرَكْنَا فِيْهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَؕ‏(37)\nWA TARAKNAA FEEHAA AAYATAL LILLAZEENA YAKHAAFOONAL A’ZAABAL ALEEM.\nand We have left therein a sign for those who fear a painful punishment.’\nوَفِىْ مُوْسٰۤی اِذْ اَرْسَلْنٰهُ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(38)\nWA FEE MOOSAA IZ ARSALNAAHO ELAA FIR-A’WNA BE-SULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nAnd in Moses [too there is a sign] when We sent him to Pharaoh with a manifest authority.\nفَتَوَلّٰى بِرُكْنِهٖ وَقَالَ سٰحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‏(39)\nFA-TAWALLAA BE-RUKNEHI WA QAALA SAAHERUN AW MAJNOON.\nBut he turned away assured of his might, and said, ‘A magician or a crazy man!’\nفَاَخَذْنٰهُ وَجُنُوْدَهٗ فَنَبَذْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ وَهُوَ مُلِيْمٌؕ‏(40)\nFA-AKHAZNAAHO WA JONOODAHU FA-NABAZNAAHUM FIL YAMME WA HOWA MOLEEM.\nSo We seized him and his hosts, and cast them into the sea, while he was blameworthy.\nوَفِىْ عَادٍ اِذْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيْحَ الْعَقِيْمَ‌ۚ‏(41)\nWA FEE A’ADIN IZ ARSALNAA A’LAYHEMUR REEHAL A’QEEM.\nAnd in ‘Ad when We unleashed upon them a barren wind.\nمَا تَذَرُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ اَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ اِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيْمِؕ‏(42)\nMAA TAZARO MIN SHAY-IN ATAT A’LAYHE ILLAA JA-A’LATHO KAR-RAMEEM.\nIt left nothing that it came upon without making it like decayed bones.\nوَفِىْ ثَمُوْدَ اِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ تَمَتَّعُوْا حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(43)\nWA FEE SAMOODA IZ QEELA LAHUM TAMATTA-O’O HATTAA HEEN.\nAnd in Thamud, when they were told, ‘Enjoy for a while.’\nفَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصّٰعِقَةُ وَ هُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ‏(44)\nFA-A’TAW A’N AMRE RABBEHIM FA-AKHAZATHOMUS SAA-E’QATO WA HUM YANZOROON.\nThen they defied the command of their Lord; so the thunderbolt seized them as they looked on.\nفَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا مِنْ قِيَامٍ وَّمَا كَانُوْا مُنْتَصِرِيْنَۙ‏(45)\nFAMAS TATAA-O’O MIN QEYAAMINW WA MAA KAANOO MUNTASEREEN.\nSo they were neither able to rise up, nor to come to one another’s aid.\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIM MIN QABL, INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nAnd the people of Noah aforetime. Indeed, they were a transgressing lot.\nوَ السَّمَآءَ بَنَيْنٰهَا بِاَيْٮدٍ وَّاِنَّا لَمُوْسِعُوْنَ‏(47)\nWAS SAMAAA-A BANAYNAAHAA BE-AYDINW WA INNAA LA-MOOSE-O’ON.\nWe have built the heaven with might, and indeed it is We who are its expanders.\nوَالْاَرْضَ فَرَشْنٰهَا فَنِعْمَ الْمٰهِدُوْنَ‏(48)\nWAL ARZA FARASHNAAHAA FA-NE’MAL MAAHEDOON.\nAnd We have spread out the earth, so how excellent spreaders We have been!\nوَمِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقْنَا زَوْجَيْنِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA MIN KULLE SHAY-IN KHALAQNAA ZAWJAYNE LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nIn all things We have created pairs so that you may take admonition.\nفَفِرُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(50)\nFA-FIRROO ELAL LAAH, INNEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\n‘So flee toward Allah. Indeed, I am from Him a manifest warner to you.\nوَلَا تَجْعَلُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ‌ؕ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ۚ‏(51)\nWA LAA TAJ-A’LOO MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHAR, INNEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nDo not set up another god besides Allah. Indeed I am from Him a manifest warner to you.’\nكَذٰلِكَ مَاۤ اَتَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا قَالُوْا سَاحِرٌ اَوْ مَجْنُوْنٌ‌ۚ‏(52)\nKAZAALEKA MAA ATAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM MIR RASOOLIN ILLAA QAALOO SAAHERUN AW MAJNOON.\nSo it was that there did not come any apostle to those who were before them but they said, ‘A magician,’ or ‘A crazy man!’\nاَتَوَاصَوْا بِهٖ‌ۚ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nATAWAASAW BEH, BAL HUM QAWMUN TAAGHOON.\nDid they enjoin this upon one another?! Rather, they were a rebellious lot.\nفَتَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمَلُوْمٍ‏(54)\nFA-TAWALLA A’NHUM FAMAA ANTA BE-MALOOM.\nSo turn away from them, as you will not be blameworthy.\nوَّذَكِّرْ فَاِنَّ الذِّكْرٰى تَنْفَعُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(55)\nWA ZAKKIR FA-INNAZ ZIKRAA TANFA-U’L MOAMENEEN.\nAnd admonish, for admonition indeed benefits the faithful.\nوَمَا خَلَقْتُ الْجِنَّ وَالْاِنْسَ اِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\nWA MAA KHALAQTUL JINNA WAL INSA ILLAA LE-YA’BODOON.\nI did not create the jinn and the humans except that they may worship Me.\nمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ وَّمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّطْعِمُوْنِ‏(57)\nMAA OREEDO MINHUM MIR RIZQINW WA MAA OREEDO AN-Y YUT-E’MOON.\nI desire no provision from them, nor do I desire that they should feed Me.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الرَّزَّاقُ ذُو الْقُوَّةِ الْمَتِيْنُ‏(58)\nINNAL LAAHA HOWAR RAZZAAQO ZUL QUWWATIL MATEEN.\nIndeed it is Allah who is the All-provider, Powerful and All-strong.\nفَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذَنُوْبًا مِّثْلَ ذَنُوْبِ اَصْحٰبِهِمْ فَلَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنِ‏(59)\nFA-INNA LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZANOOBAM MISLA ZANOOBE ASHAABEHIM FALAA YASTA’JELOON.\nIndeed the lot of those who do wrong [now] will be like the lot of their [earlier] counterparts. So let them not ask Me to hasten on [that fate].\nفَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ يَّوْمِهِمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(60)\nFA-WAYLUL LILLAZEENA KAFAROO MIN-Y YAWMEHEMUL LAZEE YOO-A’DOON.\nWoe to the faithless for the day they are promised!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zaareyaat (The Scatterers)\nThere are 60 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan it is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of moving winds or breezes.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah increases ones sustenance and makes it easy to earn. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved after being written acts as a remedy for back problems (e.g. backaches). If a pregnant woman wears a talisman of Surah al-Zaareyaat, her pregnancy and delivery will be easy. Keeping this Surah close to a dying person makes his death easy."
}
